# Independent static review: full historical complex-network GF(2)

Date: 2026-10-28. **STATIC CLEARANCE FOR ONE GUARDED PROFILE/ANCHOR ATTEMPT.** No open source blocker remains in the final driver. This is not a runtime PASS, a cost admission or permission to skip PLAN's subsequent gates. The parent remains the sole scientific runner.

Reviewed driver: `source-design/full_driver.py`, 356 lines, SHA-256 `0d976d2eb6b845f20d4a3396591a806f966688b88693cd6a5f8a0c9e48925e36`. Design SHA-256: `609a4c6aee119ddaed9f10dc2726ece18436179ad9caaced70cebaa58066f8eb`. Source inventory SHA-256: `88bba3caf5975f30fa7abceaea9454110cf3b069233e8241a2ca13d1dff171a7`.

## Scope and complete caller

[PLAN.json](PLAN.json), lines 2–12 and 24–41, defines the full H25 historical conditional CLI at main `19fdb086ea96af9a9f87936a2b888e10af4ed810`, with PR5929's native predecessor. This is separate from the blocked further-15% PR5864 task and current selected-frontier replay.

The untouched [complex_network.py](frozen/scripts/complex_network.py), lines 90–112, performs side-map, label and role checks, counts, logarithm enclosure, strict saving comparison, parameters, guard/recurrence/constraint/margin checks, dyadic/ceiling checks, source verification and gate bound. Lines 115–120 perform the actual JSON file write and two stdout lines. The driver executes this complete file through `runpy.run_path(..., run_name='__main__')`, not `witness_only()` or the former side-only harness ([driver](source-design/full_driver.py), lines 257–274).

Every full mode requires normal assertion execution (driver lines 144–146). The original assertions in [complex_circuit.py](frozen/scripts/complex_circuit.py), including map checks at 313–333, labels at 335–348 and forward/reverse role checks at 376–411, remain in the executed functions. No other imported module's `__main__` search/certificate is invoked.

## Sources, imports and the real verifier

The frozen inventory contains twelve scripts, the upstream manifest and all **19** payloads. The driver authenticates the pinned inventory, exact file sets and contents; then cross-checks the manifest's commit, payload set and each digest against that inventory (lines 152–180). The original [certify.verify_sources](frozen/scripts/certify.py), lines 226–232, still reads and hashes every actual payload. Its observational wrapper delegates the original function, and the complete run requires exactly one original-verifier call. No stubbed verifier or cached PASS replaces it.

The seven engine/input files match published PR5929 bytes. In particular, native backend, finite controls and C kernel hashes are respectively `e473c38245c3668715b5a78dfe980b2fe3ed0d0c9b8c97c666fbae6ecf1fffd5`, `df989a831aac43cc1af95169dad8c64a7548760e6e1f96976da996703f2c8f7a`, and `e9c3c9194a08718bd1575c1cf08c6c6772d3b644c2e274c25a84a1f9249d06cc`.

Both duplicated engine source files must equal the corresponding frozen scripts (driver lines 192–194). The engine's exact loaded circuit module is registered as `complex_circuit`; afterward, the driver checks the CLI's imported class/function identities and all scientific module paths (lines 209–218 and 270–289). The circuit's alternative filesystem location is explicit and byte-bound, not an unverified replacement module.

## Observers and exact outputs

The role observer calls the original function once and returns its original result object. The depth-aware serializer delegates the original recursive serializer once per value and captures only the outer full certificate (driver lines 225–255). Original [prepare_layers.serializable](frozen/scripts/prepare_layers.py), lines 148–155, retains its recursion and conversions.

The logarithm wrapper's import order is sound: `prepare_layers` first captures its ordinary alias; `search_network.log_integer_bounds` is then wrapped; the full caller subsequently imports that wrapper for its one direct call. No other called full-certificate path adds a hidden second logarithm call. Required coarse-phase counts are checked at driver lines 280–283. These observer changes do not alter Label members or helper globals tracked by the native runtime guard.

The original certificate must match pinned reference bytes, including formatting/newline, and captured CLI stdout must match both literal lines (driver lines 267–269). Reference SHA-256 is `1f763d95c7ff163aa71d13cd82784f16665be8afb21f75e76941e2119562098f`. The exact CLI stdout is separately retained and re-emitted; the outer driver also prints clearly separate receipt metadata.

The added typed full-return representation preserves Fraction pairs, float hex values, exact primitive/container types and dictionary order (driver lines 91–110). Both arms retain the complete side structural/label/role witness and ordered rank transcript through the unchanged PR5929 writer, with its fixed hashes and 59,959 calls. The complete complement receipt requires all 238,685 ordered calls and 55,839,507 canonical bytes, with the retained digest. No sampling or replacement by rank/odd-vector predicates occurs (driver lines 295–321).

## Native and independent finite boundary

The unchanged [native backend](source-design/engine/native_backend.py), lines 113–209 and 317–386, binds source/code, effective builtins, Label/helper dispatch and native callables; detects subsequent drift before native work or fallback; and preserves unsupported types/widths through the original methods. The C kernel requires exact dictionaries and nonnegative exact integers fitting 64 bits; augmented complements require total width at most 64. It preserves first-pivot/all-row elimination and ordered complement outputs ([native_gf2.c](source-design/engine/native_gf2.c), lines 17–50 and 129–195).

Each candidate cold-builds, links and loads once, then executes the entire unchanged finite suite before the full CLI (driver lines 204–207). [finite_controls.py](source-design/engine/finite_controls.py), lines 20–61, provides a separate dense-list/modulo-two oracle; lines 124–260 check ordered results, exact types, short exhaustive cases, boundary widths, permutations, fallback/error behavior and deliberately wrong/reordered controls. Lines 296–456 retain runtime-binding and complete-stream controls. The live independent finite oracle is not replaced by the profile anchor.

## Repair, cost and remaining gates

One concrete pre-execution repair was identified: `copytree` preserves readonly directory modes, so a readonly cloned root could not create `certificates/`. The final driver makes only its fresh private runtime root `0755` before that creation (lines 182–191). Copied scientific file modes remain unchanged. Compiler temporary files stay under the new output directory (lines 168–170). Source/engine/reference/anchor bytes and before/after file modes are checked; only the expected certificate may be added to the runtime tree (lines 324–331).

Both benchmark arms pay fresh copies, imports, custody checks, the complete CLI and identical retained observations; the candidate additionally pays cold build/load and all finite controls. The parent outer wall and process-group CPU receipts are authoritative. Coarse phases are nested diagnostics and must not be summed as independent savings.

The first profile creates the source-bound full-result anchor and is excluded from performance selection. Both benchmark modes reject an absent or mismatched driver/engine/input/scientific anchor (lines 145–166 and 318–323). A successful profile must precede a separate parent headroom decision. Only then may PLAN's fixed B1,C1 gate and conditional remaining BCCBBC samples proceed, retaining every stop/failure. The 180-second, 1-GiB and aggregate caps remain unchanged. No completion, memory fit, 15% gain, formal verification, new κ or PR5864 improvement is asserted by this static clearance.

Reviewer actions were source reads, file inventories and hashes only. No scientific import, execution, compilation, timing, Git/browser operation or delegation was performed.

## Parent runtime follow-up: entry-name correction

The first parent-created entry, `stages/profile-v1/profile.py`, shadowed the standard-library `profile` module imported by the unchanged helper's `cProfile` dependency. The retained [v1 receipt](runtime/runs/full-network-profile-v1/receipt.json), lines 2–22, records STOP after 0.976437556 seconds, unchanged source bytes/modes and empty stdout; [stderr](runtime/runs/full-network-profile-v1/stderr.txt), lines 21–38, identifies the recursive import and overwrite refusal. This stopped during helper import, before circuit construction or any candidate compilation. It is a retained failed attempt, not a performance sample or evidence against the mathematics.

The parent made a separate manual entry correction in immutable `profile-v2/full_profile_entry.py`; the v2 stage contains no `profile.py`. I read that entry and verified the driver/backend/finite/C hashes above are unchanged. The driver source clearance therefore carries to the corrected entry. The corrected diagnostic was reported running; no successful profile, anchor or candidate measurement is claimed in this review. [PROFILE-v1-FAILURE.json](PROFILE-v1-FAILURE.json) retains the correction boundary.
